<body>

<div class="badge">PRODUCT OVERVIEW</div>
<h1 class="title">Provider Credentialing</h1>
<h2 class="subtitle">Track PSV, verifications and tasks — built into Medical Billing.</h2>

<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k">Document</td><td>Product Overview — Provider Credentialing</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Module</td><td>Medical Billing</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Prepared for</td><td>Internal / Stakeholder Presentation</td></tr>
</table>

<h1 class="section">Why Credentialing Matters</h1>
<p>A provider can't be billed against until their credentials are verified. Credentialing keeps every provider's licensure, certifications and background checks current — and visible in one place, next to the rest of the revenue cycle.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Compliance</b> — payers require Primary Source Verification (PSV) before a provider can be enrolled.</li>
  <li><b>Revenue protection</b> — an expired credential can mean a rejected claim; tracking expirations avoids surprises.</li>
  <li><b>Accountability</b> — every verification and task has an owner, a status and a date.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">What Gets Tracked</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Overall Status</b> — Not Started, In Progress, Verified, Expired, Rejected.</li>
  <li><b>PSV Status</b> — Pending, In Progress, Completed, with a completion date.</li>
  <li><b>Verifications</b> — NPI, State License, DEA Registration, Board Certification, Malpractice Insurance, Education/Training, Work History, Hospital Privileges, OIG &amp; SAM Exclusion Checks, CAQH Profile — each with its own status, verified date, expiration date and source.</li>
  <li><b>Tasks</b> — a checklist per provider (e.g. "Request malpractice certificate"), with an assignee, due date and status.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">The Credentialing Workflow</h1>
<table class="flow-table">
  <tr>
    <td>Provider Added</td>
    <td class="arrow">→</td>
    <td>PSV Initiated</td>
    <td class="arrow">→</td>
    <td>Verifications Tracked</td>
    <td class="arrow">→</td>
  </tr>
</table>
<table class="flow-table">
  <tr>
    <td>Tasks Assigned</td>
    <td class="arrow">→</td>
    <td>Status: Verified</td>
    <td class="arrow">→</td>
    <td>Expiration Monitored</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<hr class="page-break">

