<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Where It Lives</h1>
<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k">Location</td><td>Medical Billing → Credentialing (next to Providers)</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">List View</td><td>Provider, Overall Status, PSV Status, Verifications summary, Open Tasks, Expiration Date</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Add / Edit</td><td>Full form — provider, status, PSV, dates, a dynamic Verifications list, a dynamic Tasks list</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Access</td><td>Permission-gated (view / manage), same access-control model as the rest of Medical Billing</td></tr>
</table>

<h1 class="section">Why It Matters</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Nothing falls through the cracks</b> — expiring credentials are visible on the list before they lapse.</li>
  <li><b>One system, not a spreadsheet</b> — PSV, verifications and tasks live next to the provider record itself.</li>
  <li><b>Audit-ready</b> — every verification has a status, a source and a date.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Thank You</h1>
<p>Provider Credentialing — PSV, verifications and tasks, tracked where your billing team already works.</p>

